  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "a838cc76-edf3-4cb6-8126-d2e5ce52217c",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 340,
      "shortId": "W2W9H",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "the-framework-walks-the-childr",
      "title": "The framework walks the children — Component loses `event`, gains capture/bubble",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "The core change. After it, \"forward the event to my children\" is not a line any widget contains, so\nit is not a line any widget can omit.\n\n## Current state\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs:442` used to read:\n\n```rust\nfn event(&mut self, ev: &Event) -> Handled { route_event(&mut self.base_mut().children, ev) }\n```\n\nIt has ALREADY been replaced (2026-07-26) by `on_event_capture` + `on_event`. Nothing else has\nmoved, so the workspace does not compile: 24 widgets still define `fn event`, and `route_event`\n(component.rs:582) still calls `child.event(ev)`.\n\n## Build\n\n1. `pub fn dispatch(node: &mut dyn Component, ev: &Event) -> Handled` in component.rs — the only\n   child walk in the library:\n   - `on_event_capture(ev)`; `Yes` => stop, nobody below sees it.\n   - unless `routes_own_subtree()`, walk `base_mut().children` **in reverse** (top z-order first,\n     matching today's `route_event`), recursing through `dispatch`.\n   - `on_event(ev)`.\n2. `fn routes_own_subtree(&self) -> bool { false }` on the trait — the declared exception.\n3. Delete `route_event`, or keep it `pub(crate)` solely for the opt-out widgets to call inside their\n   own capture. Prefer deleting it: leaving it reachable is how the old habit comes back.\n4. Migrate all 24 widgets (`grep -l \"fn event(&mut self\" heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/*.rs`). The\n   compiler names every one (E0407: not a member of trait). The rule for each:\n   - state that must be current before anything below is hit-tested, a gesture that must beat any\n     child under the cursor, or a swallow => **`on_event_capture`**;\n   - anything done with an event the children declined => **`on_event`**;\n   - the `route_event(children, ev)` call itself => **delete**, the framework does it.\n5. `Select` and `Dialog` declare `routes_own_subtree() -> true` with the reason on the method, and\n   keep their existing routing verbatim inside `on_event_capture`. Do NOT rewrite them: `Select`'s\n   rows are placed children (zero-sized while closed, hit-tested from baked bounds) and `Dialog`\n   routes through `FocusManager::dispatch_trapped` / `offer_to_overlay`, which are overlay-aware\n   scans, not child walks.\n6. Every caller of `.event(&Event…)` becomes `dispatch(…)`. The compiler finds them: heca/src\n   (chrome/mod.rs:1206+, app/events.rs, realize.rs tests), heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs,\n   heca-grid-ui tests.\n\n## Edge cases that will bite\n\n- **Order flips.** Today most overriding widgets handle first and never route; `Component::event`'s\n  default routed to children and did nothing else. Under `dispatch`, own-handling runs AFTER\n  children unless it is in capture. A widget that consumed a press before its children now needs\n  capture, or its children start stealing clicks.\n- **Gates become consumes.** `ScrollRegion` only forwards a press to children *when hovered*. With\n  automatic routing that gate must be expressed as capture consuming the press, and the new failure\n  mode is over-consuming — equally silent. Test both directions.\n- `Tooltip` is transparent to events and must stay so (it only adds paint).\n- Focus-barrier widgets (`Button`, `Item`, `Choice`) are one click target and one Tab stop; children\n  must not become independently clickable.\n- `Handled::No` from `on_event_capture` must not be confused with \"not interested\" — the walk\n  continues either way.\n\n## Done when\n\n- `cargo test --workspace` green, clippy 0.\n- `heca-grid-ui/tests/pointer_delivery.rs` passes unchanged, and still FAILS when an arm is removed\n  (re-verify by deleting Dialog's release handling).\n- The USER drives the app: focus traversal, a dropdown inside a modal, the context menu, the command\n  palette, sidebar row clicks and drag, terminal viewport badge/scrollbar, pane header buttons.\n  Green tests are not verification here.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-26. User drove the app and confirmed: the scroll box (wheel, Shift+wheel, both thumbs, release outside the window, click-and-hold in the track), the dialog itself (Tab, typing, Enter, Esc, scrim), and the interactions the refactor could have broken (Select dropdown, right-click context menu, command palette, sidebar rows + pane drag, pane-header buttons). 927 tests, clippy 0.\n\n## What shipped\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs`\n- `Component::event` is GONE. Two hooks replace it: `on_event_capture` (before children, `Yes`\n  stops the walk) and `on_event` (after the children declined). Neither mentions children.\n- `pub fn dispatch(node, ev)` — the only child walk in the crate; re-exported as\n  `heca_grid_ui::dispatch`. `route_event` survives only for the widgets that own their walk.\n- `fn clips_children() -> bool` + `clipped_out()` — a NEW universal rule that came out of this:\n  a widget that clips its children does not let a press or a move outside its bounds reach them.\n  Release and wheel are deliberately NOT gated (a drag must end wherever the cursor went; the wheel\n  carries no position). This replaces `ScrollRegion`'s hand-written `if self.hovered { route }` gate\n  and is what stops scrolled-out content staying clickable where it would have been.\n\n18 of 24 widgets now declare only what they do. Six own their walk, each with the reason on the\nmethod, and `tests/pointer_delivery.rs` holds every one of them to delivering all four pointer kinds:\n- `Select` — option rows are placed children, zero-sized while closed, hit-tested from baked bounds.\n- `Dialog` — routes through the overlay-aware focus scan (`dispatch_trapped`/`offer_to_overlay`).\n- `Overlay` — a closed layer's panel must be completely inert.\n- `CommandPalette`, `ContextMenu` — rows are drawn from data, not mounted as children.\n- `ItemGroup`, `DockFrame` — they report what their own subtree did, which must happen even when the\n  header consumed the click. This was found the hard way: the first attempt put the comparison in\n  `on_event` and would have silently stopped firing the toggle.\n\n`ScrollRegion` is NOT an exception — capture takes the thumb grab and hover gate, bubble takes the\nwheel and release, so the nested-region rule (innermost hovered region wins) is now simply which hook\nthe code sits in. Its `press_capture`/`move_capture` helpers live in an inherent impl at the end of\nscroll_region.rs.\n\nCall sites: ~165 `.event(..)` converted to `dispatch(..)` across heca-grid-ui, heca and the showcase.\n\n## Re-verified\n\nDeleting `Dialog`'s `PointerReleased` arm still fails `pointer_delivery.rs` with the container and\nthe kind named — the guard did not become decorative under the new model.",
