    {
      "id": "6dfe4acd-c706-485c-91b1-8b13aa163652",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 361,
      "shortId": "3PN6N",
      "priority": 5,
      "shortName": "a-modal-freezes-hover-state-th",
      "title": "A modal freezes hover state: the pane-header tooltip appears after the pointer has left",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "# The bug\n\nClick an action button in a pane's top info bar that opens a modal. Move the mouse away. The\nbutton's **tooltip appears anyway**, over a button the pointer left, while a modal owns the screen.\n\nReported by the user 2026-07-29.\n\n# Why — the pointer stops being delivered, and hover is edge-triggered\n\n`Tooltip` decides it is hovered from `PointerMoved` **transitions**\n(`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/tooltip.rs:239-250`): entering starts a wall-clock\n`hover_since`, leaving clears it, and `shown()` (`:141`) is true once `hover_since` is older than\n`delay` (default 0.5s). It never asks \"is the pointer over me *now*\" — it only reacts to a move that\ncrosses its bounds.\n\nSo it needs a leave event to un-hover, and while a modal is open it never gets one. In\n`heca/src/app/events.rs`, the `WindowEvent::CursorMoved` arm **returns early** as soon as a modal\ntakes the move:\n\n```rust\nif crate::chrome::dispatch_modal_pointer(state, &Event::PointerMoved { pos }) {\n    return;                       // ← the header trees never hear another move\n}\n…\ncrate::chrome::chrome_dispatch_move(state, pos);\ncrate::chrome::dispatch_pane_header_move(state, pos);   // ← unreached\n```\n\nThe header's `Tooltip` therefore keeps the `hover_since` it had at the moment of the click, the\ndelay elapses, `tick` crosses the show boundary, and the bubble appears over a button nobody is\npointing at.\n\n**It is not tooltip-specific.** Every hover affordance in every non-modal retained tree freezes the\nsame way: a `Row`'s hover highlight, a `Button`'s hover fill, the `MarkerGroup` grip cue. The\ntooltip is just the one that *appears* rather than merely persisting, so it is the one that got\nnoticed. The same staleness exists after the modal closes until the user happens to move the mouse.\n\n# The fix — tell the other trees the pointer left\n\nWhen a layer takes ownership of the pointer, every tree that no longer receives moves must be told\nthe pointer is gone, exactly as a real move out of bounds would tell it. One place, all affordances.\n\nCandidate shape (decide with the maintainer):\n\n- an explicit `Event::PointerLeft` in `heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs`'s `Event` enum, broadcast to\n  the non-modal trees when an overlay opens (and to the modal's tree when it closes), OR\n- reuse `PointerMoved` with a position outside every bound — cheaper, but \"a move to nowhere\" is a\n  lie the next reader has to decode, and a widget that tracks the last position would store garbage.\n\nPrefer the explicit event: hover is a real state, and \"the pointer is no longer yours\" is a real\ntransition that today has no vocabulary.\n\nDispatch sites to cover (all in `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs`): `chrome_dispatch_move` (:3479),\n`dispatch_pane_header_move` (:1261), `dispatch_pane_viewport_move`. The overlay open/close path is\n`heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs`.\n\n# Also worth checking while here\n\n- `Tooltip` has no `visible`/`disabled` gate on `shown()` — a tooltip on a widget that becomes\n  hidden between the hover and the reveal will still paint. Same class of bug.\n- The `Attention`/`Flash` and `Row` hover paths should be verified against the same scenario rather\n  than assumed correct.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- Click a pane-header action button that opens a modal, move the mouse away: **no tooltip appears**,\n  and the button is not left in its hover state.\n- Close the modal without moving the mouse: nothing is stuck hovered anywhere.\n- A tooltip still appears normally on a plain hover with no modal open.\n- A unit test in `heca-grid-ui` holds the transition: a `Tooltip` told the pointer left does not\n  reveal, however long it waits.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings. **The USER drives it in the app** — this is hover\n  timing, which no unit test verifies.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "",
      "completedAt": "",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-29T06:14:44.166Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-29T06:14:44.166Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "62b176af-bd2a-4a62-abeb-44e0e7059596",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 394,
      "shortId": "X7SSB",
      "priority": 6,
      "shortName": "a-real-pointer-event-vocabular",
      "title": "A real pointer/event vocabulary, and framework-owned routing on Base",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "**Part 1 of 2. Part 2 is `P084(F004)/T395` (context menus declared on the widget), which builds on\nthis and must not start until Antonio has driven a build of this one.** Split decided 2026-08-06:\nthis change rewires how *all* input reaches *every* widget, in both hosts; green tests said nothing\nabout six input/layout regressions this session, and only Antonio driving the GPU app found them.\nStacking a new API on unverified routing makes the bisect surface \"the whole event system plus a new\nAPI\".\n\nAgreed with Antonio 2026-08-05/06, after a session in which every bug traced back to one root: the\nwidget event vocabulary is missing pieces, so hosts and widgets reconstruct what the event should\nhave carried — each in their own way, each silently.\n\n# Why (evidence, not theory)\n\n- `Event::PointerPressed { pos }` (heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs) **carries no button and no\n  modifiers**, so a right-click can never reach a widget. `mouse.rs:428` catches it and rebuilds\n  \"what did you click\" from a position: `container_at(pos)` → `nav_key_at(pos)` →\n  `provider.context_path(&key)` → a menu-id string → the `menu(id, builder)` registry\n  (`providers/workspaces/mod.rs:300,311`).\n- That chain broke on a missing declaration: the workspace `DockFrame` pushed its key into\n  `signals.row_nav` but never called `.nav_key(...)` (`providers/workspaces/mod.rs:~1147`).\n  `nav_key_at` (heca-grid-ui/src/nav.rs:70) reads `Base::nav_key` and nothing else, so right-click on\n  a workspace opened **no menu at all** while panes and columns worked. No error, no failing test.\n  Fixed 2026-08-06 by adding the `nav_key`; the trap is the design.\n- `Event::Scroll { delta_x, delta_y }` has **no position** — `ScrollRegion`'s own module doc admits\n  *\"`Event::Scroll` carries no position, so the router can't hit-test it\"*, so it tracks hover\n  manually to know whether a wheel is for it.\n- **Six** widgets privately re-derive hover from `bounds.contains(pos)`: `Row`, `Item`, `RailCell`,\n  `Toast`, `Button`, `ScrollRegion`. `Input` keeps its own click counter for double/triple click.\n- **Seven** widgets hand-rolled raw `Enter`/`Space` activation with no focus check — fixed 2026-08-06\n  by moving the rule into `dispatch` (`deaf_to_raw_key` + `Component::takes_raw_keys`, defaulting to\n  `routes_own_subtree`). That fix is the precedent for this task: same class, same cure.\n- `Dialog::submit` synthesised `Event::Key { Enter }` at its primary button because nothing could say\n  \"activate this child\" through `dyn Component` — fixed 2026-08-06 with `Component::activate`.\n\nAntonio: *\"I want a user that wants to build a widget to just position it and it works out of the\nbox. They should NEVER be worried of blocking things you invented.\"* / *\"we cannot ship hardcoded\nAPIs or missing ones.\"*\n\n# Decisions (settled — do not re-open)\n\n1. **Events say what happened, never what you should do about it.** `right_click`, not\n   `context_menu`. Naming an event after the intended response is the same coupling as `.action()`.\n   Shift+F10 / the Menu key can *emit* `right_click`; that needs no new event type.\n2. **Handlers live on `Base`**, like `bounds`, `children`, `focused`, `nav_key`, `style`. Every widget\n   embedding `Base` gets them with no code.\n3. **The builder side is an `EventExt` trait** — the established one-line opt-in pattern of\n   `LayoutExt` / `StyleExt` / `NavExt`.\n4. **The framework resolves the raw pointer stream once**: hit-test → target → bubble; press+release\n   on the same widget ⇒ `click`; click count ⇒ `double_click`; `contains(pos)` transitions ⇒\n   `enter`/`leave`; the button on the press ⇒ `right_click`/`middle_click`.\n5. **Target + bubbling**, with `stop_propagation()` as the opt-out and capture as a rare opt-in.\n   Today it is capture-first-wins with no way to stop or continue deliberately — exactly how a `Row`\n   swallowed an `Enter` meant for its list.\n6. **`heca-grid-ui` must not learn about the app.** Not `ViewNode`, not `AppState`, not `WmAction`.\n\n# The vocabulary\n\nPointer/buttons: `pointer_down`/`pointer_up` gain **button + modifiers**; `click`, `double_click`,\n`triple_click`, `right_click`, `middle_click`.\nPointer/movement: `pointer_enter` / `pointer_leave`.\nWheel: **position** on `Scroll`.\nKeyboard: `text_input` for typed text/IME, distinct from `Key` — `Input` reconstructs it from\n`GridKey::Char` today, which forces the host's \"deliver the actual character, not the lowercased\ncombo key\" fixup in `app/events.rs`.\nFocus: `focus` / `blur` **events** — there is a `focused` signal but no event, so nothing can act on\ngaining/losing focus (select-all on focus, commit on blur, close a dropdown when focus leaves).\nLifecycle: `mount` / `unmount`.\nDrag: `drag_start`/`drag`/`drag_end`, `drag_enter`/`drag_over`/`drag_leave`/`drop` — today drag is\nentirely app-side (`DragItemRegistry`, `mouse/drag.rs`), so a plugin widget cannot participate.\n\n**Order, by how much each removes:** button + modifiers → `right_click` → `enter`/`leave` → position\non `Scroll`. Those four delete four existing hacks; the rest completes the vocabulary.\n\n# What this deletes here\n\nSix private hover copies, `Input`'s private click counter, and the widget-side half of the\nright-click archaeology. The menu-side deletions (`context_path`, the `menu(id, builder)` registry,\nthe `MENU_*` constants, `open_row_context_menu`) belong to T395.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- `stop_propagation()` on a click must not suppress `leave` on the widget being left.\n- Double-click must still deliver the first `click` — do not swallow it waiting for a second.\n- `right_click` must not also fire `click`.\n- A widget removed from the tree between press and release must not strand a `click`.\n- Bubbling must survive `routes_own_subtree` containers (`Overlay`, `Dialog`, `ContextMenu`,\n  `CommandPalette`, `Select`, `FocusScope`, `DockFrame`, `ItemGroup`) — they route their own\n  children and must pass a bubbling event up, not eat it.\n- The pointer is **never** focus-gated (unlike raw keys): a click on an unfocused dock is how you\n  focus it.\n\n# Verification\n\nWidget-level tests are cheap and were what actually found this session's bugs — a headless dispatch\ntest proved the exposé tree was fine and moved the hunt to the app. But input behaviour needs Antonio\ndriving the GPU app: green tests said nothing about any of the six regressions. **Do not claim it\nworks.** Hand him a build and wait before starting T395.\n\nDocumentation is part of this task: the full event vocabulary, the target/bubble model, `EventExt`,\nand what a widget author has to know (which should be: nothing).\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\n**DONE 2026-08-06 — built, and driven by Antonio in the GPU app (\"its good\"). Uncommitted.**\n\n⚠️ **C7–C11 and C14 are `P084(F004)/T395`'s**, not this task's — the checklist was written before the\n2026-08-06 split and never re-cut. C1–C6, C12, C13, C15 are this one, and are done.\n\n# What shipped\n\n**One pointer event leaves a host** — `Event::Raw(RawPointer)` with the **button** and the\n**modifiers** on it. `heca-grid-ui/src/pointer.rs` (new) resolves it once: hit-test → hover diff →\npress/release pairing → click runs → drag threshold → delivery (capture down the path, bubble back\nup). No widget hit-tests a pointer event; no widget forwards one.\n\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/event.rs` (new): the vocabulary. `PointerDown/Up/Move`, `PointerEnter/Leave`,\n  `Click/DoubleClick/TripleClick`, `RightClick/MiddleClick`, `PointerDownOutside`, `Scroll` (with a\n  position), the seven drag events, `Focus`/`Blur`, `Mount`/`Unmount`, `TextInput` separate from\n  `Key`. `PointerButton`, `PointerEvent`, `DragEvent`, `EventKind`, `EventCx`, `Handlers`.\n  Re-exported from `component.rs`, so no import moved.\n- `builders.rs`: **`EventExt`** — `.on_click`, `.on_right_click`, `.on_pointer_enter`, `.on_drop`,\n  `.on(kind, |cx| cx.stop_propagation())`. Every widget, no opt-in.\n- **State lives on the widgets** (`Base::pointer: PointerState`), not in a router the host owns: the\n  ~8 trees heca mounts never share a hover or a capture, and a widget dropped mid-gesture takes its\n  own state with it.\n\n# Three `Component` hooks, each replacing a workaround\n\n- **`hit_bounds() -> Option<Rectangle>`** — input surface ≠ layout box (a menu/palette panel);\n  `None` = takes no input at all (a closed `Overlay`, still laid out). The input twin of\n  `damage_bounds`.\n- **`after_subtree(ev, handled)`** — a container observing what its own rows did, consumed or not.\n  `ItemGroup`/`DockFrame` gave back the whole child walk they had taken over to get it.\n- **Capture on press** — consuming a `PointerDown` captures the pointer. `ScrollBar`/`ScrollRegion`\n  no longer arrange to hear the rest of their own gesture.\n\n# Deleted\n\nSeven private `contains()` helpers and every private hover copy; `Input`'s click counter + clock and\n`MULTI_CLICK`; `ScrollRegion`'s manual wheel hover-gate; **both** host \"deliver the real character,\nnot the lowercased combo key\" fixups (`app/events.rs`, `app/input.rs`); pointer forwarding in\n`Overlay`/`Dialog`/`FocusScope`/`ItemGroup`/`DockFrame`; `clipped_out` in `component.rs`.\n\n# Found in his testing (2026-08-06) — both fixed and pinned\n\n1. **A right-click on a sidebar row opened no menu.** Nine widgets carried\n   `Event::PointerDown(_) => Handled::Yes` — an arm with no body that claimed **every** button, so a\n   `Row` spent the right press and `mouse.rs`'s `open_row_context_menu` was never reached (the pane\n   worked because no widget sits there). Fixed as a declaration, not nine copies:\n   **`Base::one_click_target`**, the pointer twin of `focus_barrier`, applied by the router in\n   capture, **left button only**. The nine arms are gone.\n2. **Clicking away from an open menu did not close it.** `broadcast_outside` called `on_event`\n   directly and `ContextMenu` answers in `on_event_capture`; it now goes through `deliver_self`\n   (capture → handlers → `on_event`), the same single-node delivery as enter/leave. Also: a press\n   *inside* the panel matching no row does nothing again (only an outside press dismisses).\n\n# Behaviour change he will feel\n\nControls **fire on the click, not the press** — press, drag off, release, and nothing fires. The\npress is still consumed (host \"did a widget take it\" answers unchanged) and the click goes to\nwhoever took the press, so composed content cannot steal it.\n\n# Verification\n\n1216 tests, clippy 0 warnings. `heca-grid-ui/tests/pointer_routing.rs` (new, 23 tests) holds the\nresolution to the spec, including every edge case the task named: a leave no neighbour can veto; the\nfirst click never held back (a run *adds* `DoubleClick` on top of `Click`); a right-click that never\nalso fires a click; a widget removed between press and release; bubbling through every container\nthat used to own its walk; a control taking the left press and letting every other button past.\n`tests/pointer_delivery.rs` reworked to the resolved vocabulary.\n\n# Documentation\n\nRustdoc throughout, including a long entry on **`Handled`** at his explicit request (\"must be well\ndocumented otherwise noone will know how to work\"): the DOM comparison (`stopPropagation` +\n`preventDefault` in one), the third meaning the DOM lacks (the *host* reads the accumulated answer\nto decide whether the terminal gets the input), the three jobs a `Yes` on a `PointerDown` does, a\nwhich-answer-to-give table, and the events whose answer is ignored. `docs/widgets.md`: the event\nmodel rewritten, `EventExt` + `one_click_target` in the builder tables, the `Component` table, the\nhost wiring recipe. `AGENTS.md`: a SETTLED block so none of it is re-derived.\n\n# Files\n\nNew: `heca-grid-ui/src/event.rs`, `src/pointer.rs`, `tests/pointer_routing.rs`. Touched: every\nwidget in `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/`, `component.rs`, `builders.rs`, `focus.rs`, `layout.rs`,\n`keymap.rs`, `lib.rs`; `heca/src/app/events.rs`, `app/input.rs`, `chrome/mod.rs`, `mouse.rs`;\n`heca-view-realize/src/lib.rs`; `heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs`.",
