    {
      "id": "5ef43ba4-d6c8-482f-a908-40b1426a19e3",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 395,
      "shortId": "BLRSH",
      "priority": 7,
      "shortName": "context-menus-declared-on-the",
      "title": "Context menus declared on the widget — a ContextMenu value, a host sink, and one generalised action",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "**Part 2 of 2. `P084(F004)/T394` (the event vocabulary + framework-owned routing) is DONE and driven by Antonio in the app, 2026-08-06.**\n\n# ⚠️ THE API IS DECIDED — do not re-open, do not \"improve\"\n\nAntonio rejected three designs before this one. **Rejected, so nobody rebuilds them:** `path` / `target` / `about` on the menu; `alter_menus`; `MenuPath::declare`; `MenuRow::at`; `fn context_menus() -> Vec<…>` (*\"why a function that return vec?? still the same as before.. WHY?? i want simple APIs\"*); and a `MenuPanel` type that was invented rather than asked about (*\"YOU HAVE TO ASK AND NOT TO INVENT\"*).\n\nThe full model is now in **`AGENTS.md` → ⭐ SETTLED — the menu model** and **`docs/widgets.md` → Menus**. Read those, not this section, for the rules.\n\n**The type is named `ContextMenu`** — decided by Antonio 2026-08-07 when asked (the handoff had written `ContextualMenu`).\n\n**Composed content is a shared builder** (`Rc<dyn Fn() -> Box<dyn Component>>`), chosen by Antonio 2026-08-07 from three options put to him. It makes `MenuItem` / `Menu` / `ContextMenu` all `Clone` — so `.context_menu()` takes **a value or a closure** (`IntoContextMenu`) — while each opening still gets **owned** children that go through the normal layout path. The rejected alternative (`Rc<dyn Component>` shared *widgets*) would have forced a second layout implementation inside the menu widget.\n\n# BUILT AND GREEN (uncommitted; 1232 tests, clippy clean)\n\n## The library\n\n- `MenuItem::new()` (no args) + `.label()` / `.icon()` sugar + `.child(|| widget)` composed content, **children win**; `.key/.shortcut/.danger/.enabled/.on_click` apply to both forms.\n- `Menu` — title, description, optional `.name()`, items; `Clone`.\n- `ContextMenu::new(id).child(menu)` — the named presenter, **and the panel**. Rows are realized into `Base::children` at open, so **taffy lays them out**; the widget's only geometry is `place_panel()` shifting the finished panel to its anchor (the `shift_subtree` trick `Overlay`/`Select` use). The hand-rolled width/row-height maths is gone.\n- Row colour resolved at paint and published with `PaintCx::with_content_color`, so a composed row reads danger / dims when disabled without knowing about menus. Keycap + shortcut stay panel chrome, painted into space the row reserves via `MenuItem::trailing_width`.\n- `Event::position()` and `Event::target_bounds()`; the latter stamped **once** by `pointer::deliver_targeted`, so every routed pointer event carries the delivery target's bounds and no widget arranges its own. `MenuAnchor::from_event` reads the anchor; `ContextMenu::show(ev)` is the handler road.\n- `EventExt::context_menu(value | closure)`; `context_menu_built` removed. `Base::context_menu: Option<Box<dyn Fn() -> ContextMenu>>`.\n- `LayoutExt::max_width` / `max_height` — `Style::max_width` was already wired to taffy and had no builder.\n- Tests: `heca-grid-ui/tests/context_menu_declaration.rs`, **13** — the original 8 plus value-vs-closure, one value on every row of a list, a composed row surviving a second opening, composed-beats-sugar with both forms measured by the engine, and the anchor coming out of the event.\n\n## The app\n\n- The **three sidebar menus are declared on their rows** (`pane_card`, `column_view`, the workspace `DockFrame`), built where the row's data is.\n- **Root menu for empty space**: `MENU_CONTAINER` on the container's `ScrollRegion` — a click between rows / below the last / on padding bubbles out to \"New workspace\". No empty-space hit test.\n- `chrome::context_menu::menu_from_items` — the shared bridge from the `DropdownItem` vocabulary to a declared `Menu`. Icons from the action (`ctx.action_icon`), behaviour as `InteractionIntent::View(Intent)` through the **central gate**, `name` for contributions.\n- **`ChromeCtx::action_icon(name)`** + the catalog on `RenderInputs`. Needed because the nine ids those menus use (`close`, `delete_column`, `rename_pane`, …) are **built-ins**, not the provider's own actions — the provider declares `cursor_up` / `activate_row` / `rename_row`. A narrow accessor, not the whole catalog.\n- `open_context_menu` **generalised**: asks the focused *widget* first via `chrome::open_declared_menu_for_focus` → `heca_grid_ui::open_for_focused` (bubbling), falling back to the content-pane path, which stays because a terminal surface is not a widget that can carry a declaration.\n- **Deleted**: `Provider::context_menus` for workspaces, `context_path`, `build_pane_row_menu` / `build_column_row_menu` / `build_workspace_row_menu`, `open_row_context_menu` (mouse.rs) and its position archaeology. `Provider::context_menus` **stays on the trait** — it is the plugin contribution path (`plugin_providers_for`).\n- Showcase shows **both row forms in one menu** on purpose (four sugar rows + a composed \"Close\" of `Icon` + `Label` + `Badge`).\n- Docs: `docs/widgets.md` → a new **Menus** section replacing the old `ContextMenu` one (9 stale anchors re-pointed, ToC entry added); `AGENTS.md` ⭐ SETTLED block.\n\n# 🔴 THE BUG ANTONIO FOUND, AND ITS LESSON\n\n**Right-clicking a sidebar row opened nothing.** Found by him in the running app on the day the port landed, with the whole suite green.\n\n`Event::RightClick` is synthesised from a press **and** a release on the same widget. `heca/src/mouse.rs` had only ever dispatched the right-button **press** into the chrome tree. That never mattered before, because `open_row_context_menu` ran straight after the press and opened the menu from the cursor position — and this task **deleted** that function. So the declared menus that replaced it could never fire: not half a click, **no** click.\n\n**Why nothing failed:** `context_menu_declaration.rs` dispatches press *and* release itself. Every test passed while the app sent one half.\n\nFixed with a `(MouseButton::Right, ElementState::Released)` branch + `chrome::chrome_dispatch_button_release`. **Guard added**: `the_mouse_layer_sends_a_release_for_every_press_it_sends` in `heca/tests/pointer_funnel.rs` — that file already lints the event loop for exactly this class of absence, and none of its checks read `mouse.rs`, the *second* place a button reaches the chrome tree.\n\n# What is LEFT\n\n1. **`Shift+F10` and the `Menu` key — BLOCKED, and this is the only unfinished piece of the API.**\n   `GridKey` has no function keys and no Menu key (its variants: `ArrowUp/Down/Left/Right`, `Backspace`, `Char`, `Delete`, `End`, `Enter`, `Escape`, `Home`, `Space`, `Tab`, and the mouse buttons). Both bindings need the **key vocabulary** extended first: a `GridKey` variant, the winit mapping in `heca/src/app/events.rs`, and the config parser (`heca/src/input.rs::parse_key`) accepting `f10` / `menu`. Open design question for Antonio: `GridKey::F(u8)` vs `F1..F12` variants, and what the Menu key is spelled as in config.\n   `prefix+>` works and is unchanged; the action it fires is already the generalised one, so the two extra bindings are **config lines** once the keys exist.\n2. **Antonio drives a build.** Right-click a pane, a column, a workspace header, empty sidebar space; `prefix+>` with focus on a sidebar row; the showcase's composed row beside its sugar rows. **Do not claim it works** — the one thing that went wrong here was invisible to 1232 green tests.\n\n# Then, in his order\n\n- **`Button` composed content / ViewNode** — *\"we need to also rewrite that button to be a ViewNode at the end but first handle this\"*.\n- **DnD**: `P079(F004)/T318` (rewritten to **delete** `DragSurfaceId`, not extend it) and `T396`. `T330` is rejected.\n- Filed while working on this, both in P084: **T397** (the complete Phosphor iconset + a generated name↔`Glyph` mapping — ~1,500 icons already ship in the binary, 52 are reachable) and **T398** (plugins must be able to build EVERY widget — 32 `WidgetKind`s for ~70 exported types; `Menu`/`MenuItem` are its first slice).",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [
        {
