    {
      "id": "8f13b870-62c4-4556-a33f-377073527b4f",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 397,
      "shortId": "2PVMF",
      "priority": 8,
      "shortName": "the-complete-phosphor-iconset",
      "title": "The complete Phosphor iconset + a generated name↔Glyph mapping",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "**Filed 2026-08-07 from `BACKLOG.md:1718` (`plugin-task-ui-8`), which was never in the planner.** It came up while deciding where a context-menu row's icon comes from (T395) and where a *plugin's* icon could come from. Transferred here in full; the backlog entry's two stale details are corrected below.\n\n# Why this is small, and why it unlocks a lot\n\n**~1,500 icons already ship in the binary and 52 are reachable.** The embedded face\n`heca-grid-ui/assets/Phosphor-Duotone.ttf` (family `Phosphor-Duotone`, MIT, loaded via\n`ICON_FONT_BYTES` at `heca-grid-ui/src/font.rs:56`) has **3025 codepoints** — measured with\n`fontTools`, not estimated. Phosphor Duotone pairs each icon consecutively\n(`PRIMARY_OFFSET = 1`, `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/icon.rs:27`), so that is roughly **1,512 icons**.\nThe `Glyph` enum (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/icon.rs:33`) exposes **52** — about 3%.\n\nSo \"a plugin wants a Docker whale / a database / a cloud\" needs **no new font, no new asset, no\nlicensing question**: the glyph is already in the binary. The only thing missing is a way to *name*\nit. That is this task.\n\nThis is also why **Nerd Font is the wrong answer** for pictograms: `FontRole::NerdFont`\n(`heca-grid-ui/src/scene.rs:325`) exists for the keyboard glyphs Phosphor has none of (`⇧ ⌘ ⎋`),\nand routing plugin icons through it would put plugin UI in a different visual language from the app.\n\n# Current state\n\n- `Glyph` — a hand-transcribed curated enum, 52 variants, `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/icon.rs:33`.\n  `secondary()` gives the `:before` codepoint; `primary_char()` adds `PRIMARY_OFFSET`.\n- `glyph_from_name` — the name→`Glyph` lookup the declarative path uses, at\n  **`heca-view-realize/src/lib.rs:1077`** (the backlog says `heca/src/chrome/realize.rs`; it moved\n  when the model became its own crate). Its own doc calls it \"a **curated stopgap of ~35 icons**\"\n  (the enum is now 52 — the two already disagree, which is the drift this task exists to end).\n- `heca-renderer/tests/font_coverage.rs` — reads the embedded faces' `cmap` and fails the build when\n  a named codepoint has no glyph. Hand-maintained today.\n- **The transcription has already been wrong once**: `Glyph::PlusSquare` was removed because its\n  codepoint drew something else, and `CaretLeft`/`CaretUp` still carry \"confirm visually\" comments —\n  because, per the P085 handoff, *\"the Phosphor codepoint table is not in the repo\"*.\n\n# What to build\n\n1. **Get Phosphor's name↔codepoint table into the repo.** It ships with the Phosphor release (the\n   CSS/JSON map). This single piece of data is the whole unlock — everything below is generated\n   from it.\n2. **Generate** the `Glyph` enum (or its codepoint table) **and** the name lookup from that one\n   source — build script, macro or generated table. The backlog's words: *\"a hand-maintained 1:1\n   match of hundreds of icons is a bug farm.\"* The enum and `glyph_from_name` must not be able to\n   diverge.\n3. **`Icon::new(\"name\")` in grid-ui.** Today `Icon::new` takes the `Glyph` enum\n   (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/icon.rs:224`) and the only name lookup lives in `heca-view-realize`,\n   **above** grid-ui, so grid-ui cannot reach it. With a generated table the lookup can live in\n   grid-ui and `heca-view-realize` can drop its stopgap and call it.\n   ⚠️ **Do not silently swap `Glyph` for a string.** A `Glyph` typo is a compile error; a name typo\n   resolves to `None` and draws nothing — the same invisible failure as the missing `.nav_key(..)`\n   that opened no menu with no error and no failing test. Decide with Antonio whether the string\n   form is additive (both) or a replacement.\n4. **Turn `font_coverage` into a check over the generated data** rather than a hand-written list, so\n   every generated name is proven present in the embedded `cmap`.\n5. **Document the names for authors** — `docs/widgets.md` icon table, `docs/chrome-and-ui.md` — and\n   update the showcase icon gallery.\n6. **Plugin registration validates at registration time.** A plugin naming an icon cannot be caught\n   by a build-time test, so the registration path must reject an unknown name rather than let the\n   renderer draw an empty box.\n\n# Ordering\n\nThe backlog's condition — *\"Run this last in the plugin arc, once the widget/`realize`/overlay\nsurface is settled, so the iconset is filled against the final set of consumers\"* — is met by T395,\nwhich settles the menu/overlay surface. It is filed here for that reason.\n\n# Not in scope, deliberately\n\nFonts a plugin ships itself (`FontRole` would stop being a closed enum and become a font registry:\nloading, ids, duplicate families, licensing, atlas lifetime) and arbitrary image/SVG icons (a\ntexture path, not a glyph — `heca-renderer/src/image.rs` exists for kitty graphics but nothing wires\nit to widgets). Both are real features, not extensions of this one.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- Duotone means **two** codepoints per icon; a generated table must carry the secondary and derive\n  the primary via `PRIMARY_OFFSET`, not assume one codepoint per name.\n- The embedded face's range runs to `U+EE83` and includes non-icon codepoints (the count starts at\n  `U+0000`) — generate from Phosphor's own map, not by walking the `cmap`.\n- Expanding `Glyph` to ~1,500 variants makes any exhaustive `match` on it unmaintainable; check for\n  existing exhaustive matches (`Glyph::ALL`-style walks, the coverage guard, any icon picker) before\n  expanding, and prefer a table to enum variants where a match would otherwise explode.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
